            <h2>2. 2026 IVF Technology: PGT-A, Time-Lapse Embryo Monitoring & IMSI</h2>

            <p>Chinese fertility leaders have invested heavily in cutting-edge reproductive technology. Three advances in particular have transformed success rates and driven international patient growth:</p>

            <div class="tech-card">
                <h4>PGT-A (Preimplantation Genetic Testing for Aneuploidies)</h4>
                <p>PGT-A screens embryos for chromosomal abnormalities before transfer. In 2026, Chinese top clinics achieve <strong>85-92% accuracy</strong> in identifying euploid (genetically normal) embryos. This reduces miscarriage risk by up to 50% and improves live birth rates per transfer to <strong>65-72%</strong> for women under 35. PGT-A is particularly recommended for women over 35, couples with recurrent miscarriage, or those with previous IVF failures.</p>
                <p><strong>2026 Cost add-on:</strong> $800–$1,500 on top of base IVF cycle</p>
            </div>

            <div class="tech-card">
                <h4>Time-Lapse Embryo Monitoring (EmbryoScope® / ESI)</h4>
                <p>Time-lapse incubators capture thousands of images of developing embryos without removing them from the incubator. AI-powered algorithms analyze cell division patterns, multinucleation, and cleavage timing to rank embryo viability. Studies show time-lapse selection improves clinical pregnancy rates by <strong>15-20%</strong> compared to conventional grading. All top Chinese clinics adopted this technology by 2024; by 2026 it is standard at premium centers.</p>
                <p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Fewer transfers, faster path to pregnancy, reduced cryopreservation costs</p>
            </div>

            <div class="tech-card">
                <h4>IMSI (Intracytoplasmic Morphologically Selected Sperm Injection)</h4>
                <p>IMSI uses a high-magnification (6,000x) microscope to examine sperm morphology before injection, selecting only sperm with normal nuclear shape and intact DNA. For couples with male factor infertility or recurrent IVF failure, IMSI improves fertilization rates by <strong>10-15%</strong> and reduces embryo arrest. Some clinics combine IMSI with PICSI (physiological ICSI) for double sperm selection.</p>
                <p><strong>2026 Cost add-on:</strong> $300–$700 on top of ICSI</p>
            </div>

